{"id":"398045447","kind":"article","title":"间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2021-08-09","updated":"2023-07-12","votes":21,"comment_count":4,"minutes":3,"chars":1285,"keywords":["间隔重复","概念理解","记忆卡片","测试效应","知识迁移","卡片编写"],"summary":"Andy Matuschak 指出，间隔重复不只适合记名称、定义等简单事实；自行编写的卡片也可以围绕联系、原因、影响和后果，帮助学习者内化复杂概念并持续琢磨高层次关系。概念卡片更难设计，但测试效应也适用于概念性知识；作者还提出，这类材料可能适合更长的复习间隔。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/398045447","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"Ue-ycfpm\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>显然可以用来记忆简单事实：名称、定义、数字常数等。记忆系统的绝大多数使用者似乎只将其用于这一目的。但是，间隔重复并不仅限于对记忆简单事实有用。如果你自己写卡片，它还可以用来深入理解复杂的材料（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5TxQNCUTSAiTg42v7Ft6xASpnyiuvm6phAoJ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">亲自间隔重复记忆卡片有多重要？</a>）。这种面向概念的卡片可能会从联系、影响、原因、后果出发问问题。这些更广泛的想法乍一看根本不是可以记忆的事实，但其实是的。使用间隔重复系统，不仅能让你记住这些概念性的想法，还能让你琢磨更高层次的关系，从而与话题保持联系，更深刻地内化材料。（相关笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7tjqSxGsJ53tXsGkRpchsECWcMsW3sFUw86U\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介使读者与材料保持长久联系</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>）</p><p data-pid=\"95N_H_C2\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ntJ7w9C3uapYp1m3gy2EK6PN788guzEoUNN\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>；写好概念性卡片就更难了。对于编码抽象而概念性的知识的技术，还没有深入而广为接受的见解。欲了解更多，请参见<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z42J1vxsMjhkdbrqVfoqjiEesSzfaEqurBtoJ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">高质量的间隔重复记忆卡片最重要的属性是什么？</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。特别相关：《<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3K5a9tM1wq1x4QnDfsUpTeYZWW3M9iUzMdfo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆卡片应该从多个角度对概念进行编码</a>》<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"cxcfFOwE\">间隔重复系统对概念性理解的发展功能，有力反驳了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zD5zaKmvTFAAL3PTJGWzkAQr6CtoBCdoXBpM\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作并不重要</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>的看法。</p><p data-pid=\"xtI2O12H\">值得注意的是，间隔重复的认知心理学基础（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup>）已被证明适用于概念性知识以及陈述性知识（见 Karpicke 和 Blunt，2011）。</p><p data-pid=\"lfP9GAG2\">有可能这种类型的信息用间隔重复的时间安排来记忆会更「便宜」：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5fqaiYdbfoGyKF4KU8MV7MFPFe467n2a5LAP\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概念性信息可能有更慢的最佳间隔重复时间表</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><hr/><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\"><b>参考文献</b></h2><p data-pid=\"HS0PXewM\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zKhfH8c9tyT3e8sZzDSKZ3yMmLFjybUT1CA\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Butler, A. (2010). Repeated Testing Produces Superior Transfer of Learning Relative to Repeated Studying. Journal of Experimental Psychology. Learning, Memory, and Cognition, 36, 1118–1133.</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup></p><p data-pid=\"8cg0aJ5T\">Matuschak, A., &amp; Nielsen, M. (2019, October 0). <i>How can we develop transformative tools for thought?</i><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-10\"><a href=\"#ref-10\">[10]</a></sup> <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">numinous.productions/tt</span><span class=\"invisible\">ft</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a> (see section “<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft/#how-important-is-memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">How important is memory anyway?</a>”)</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"mExB8bBJ\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"398094270\" href=\"#/post/398094270\">高质量的间隔重复记忆卡片最重要的属性是什么？</a></li><li data-pid=\"89csAY4u\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"408715726\" href=\"#/post/408715726\">我的间隔重复系统方法的不同之处</a></li><li data-pid=\"tEnjVRwf\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"454266265\" href=\"#/post/454266265\">许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要</a></li><li data-pid=\"Eu10Lo7s\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"464129684\" href=\"#/post/464129684\">助记媒介如何帮助读者建立更复杂的理解？</a></li><li data-pid=\"liDX4zPm\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"468172742\" href=\"#/post/468172742\">间隔重复记忆系统让记忆更加自动化，从而有助于更深入的琢磨思考</a></li><li data-pid=\"CPKHPmlQ\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"565182669\" href=\"#/post/565182669\">概念型知识的「最优复习间隔」可能更长</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"Mo8TqtzN\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"YaB45-5T\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Spaced repetition memory systems can be used to develop conceptual understanding</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 助记媒介使读者与材料保持长久联系 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"464712237\" href=\"#/post/464712237\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397245681\" href=\"#/post/397245681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 高质量的间隔重复记忆卡片最重要的属性是什么？ <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"398094270\" href=\"#/post/398094270\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆卡片应该从多个角度对概念进行编码 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"401463758\" href=\"#/post/401463758\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"454266265\" href=\"#/post/454266265\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 测试效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"423449068\" href=\"#/post/423449068\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 概念型知识的「最优复习间隔」可能更长 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"565182669\" href=\"#/post/565182669\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 相较于重复学习，重复测试的迁移学习效果更好 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"604132912\" href=\"#/post/604132912\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-10\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-10\">↩</a> 我们如何才能开发出变革性的思想工具？ <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"394795804\" href=\"#/post/394795804\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"397582470","title":"间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"398094270","title":"高质量的间隔重复记忆卡片最重要的属性是什么？","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":36,"minutes":3,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"397245681","title":"写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"464712237","title":"助记媒介使读者与材料保持长久联系","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":16,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"464129684","title":"助记媒介如何帮助读者建立更复杂的理解？","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":13,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2783974335","title":"我们常说记忆时要学会理解记忆，不要死记硬背，那到底什么才是真正的理解记忆？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":121,"minutes":56,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 121 赞同","evidence":"正文通过明确题名/术语锚点“叶峻峣：间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解”原生链接到目标译文，摘要与周边讨论相符。"},{"id":"2834169225","title":"如何学会正确的理解记忆？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":32,"minutes":7,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 32 赞同","evidence":"回答含指向该译文的原生引用锚点，可唯一定位到该标题/关键词。"}]}